        "original_id": "de0ffd6a-849f-5f0f-a4fb-97e6b1c6368e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joel Chandler Harris, James Baskett\n- Characters: Uncle Remus, Br'er Rabbit\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company\n- Works: Song of the South, Uncle Remus stories, \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah\"\n\nFacts:\n- Joel Chandler Harris adapted the Uncle Remus stories.\n- In 1946, The Walt Disney Company adapted Br'er Rabbit for the animated motion picture Song of the South.\n- In 1946, Song of the South was based on the collection of Uncle Remus stories as adapted by Joel Chandler Harris.\n- In 1946, James Baskett starred in the Disney feature film Song of the South as Uncle Remus and sang the song \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah.\"\n- James Baskett was an American actor born on February 16, 1904, and he died on July 9, 1948.\n- James Baskett was known for portraying Uncle Remus.",
